OpenRFID — QIDI / Anycubic / Elegoo / Creality tag format support
-----------------------------------------------------------------
The QIDI, Anycubic, Elegoo, and Creality tag processors and lookup
tables (under
`app/src/main/java/com/spoolpainter/app/hardware/nfc/vendor/`) are
ported from the OpenRFID project:

  https://github.com/suchmememanyskill/OpenRFID

Specifically, the source files at
`OpenRFID/src/tag/{qidi,anycubic,elegoo,creality}/` at upstream commit
`ddd1609e9abe9cd37c4b8fa1a0e4307b976d5fd4` were translated to Kotlin
in this repository. OpenRFID is published under GPL-3.0; SpoolPainter
inherits and remains under GPL-3.0 as a result.

OpenRFID — vendor tag test fixtures
-----------------------------------
The vendor tag dumps and their expected-output sidecars under
`app/src/test/resources/vendor-fixtures/{Elegoo,Anycubic,Qidi,Snapmaker,Bambu}/`
(`*.bin` raw chip captures + `*.yml` expected decode results) are copied
verbatim from `OpenRFID/test/tags/` at the same upstream commit
`ddd1609e9abe9cd37c4b8fa1a0e4307b976d5fd4`. They are used solely as
regression test data for the vendor tag processors. Creality fixtures
are not included — they require a per-tag AES encryption key that
upstream supplies via environment variable, not in the repository.

